      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(baseten): reject malformed model metadata numbers",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nBaseten live model discovery trusted JavaScript numeric string forms from `/models` metadata. A malformed string such as `0x100000` or `3.2e4` could be accepted through `Number(...)` and override curated context-window, max-token, or pricing metadata instead of falling back to the bundled catalog values.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nLive metadata now accepts JSON numbers as before, but string metadata must be canonical decimal syntax before it is parsed. Invalid numeric strings are ignored, so the existing fallback metadata remains authoritative for malformed live rows.\n\n## User Impact\n\nBaseten model catalogs no longer surface inflated or malformed live context windows, token limits, or per-token prices when the provider response contains non-decimal numeric strings.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Current head: `175639afcba20f864b3b9232e6c6342522c415cf`.\n- Provider-boundary transcript at the Baseten discovery seam passed for the current head: `discoverBasetenModels` used a redacted fetch guard for `https://inference.baseten.co/v1/models` with `Authorization: Bearer <redacted>`.\n- The transcript fed a malformed `thinkingmachines/inkling` row with `context_length: \"0x100000\"`, `max_completion_tokens: \"3.2e4\"`, and malformed price strings `\"0x1\"`, `\"4.2e-6\"`, and `\" 0.00000018 \"`; the projected model kept bundled fallback values `contextWindow: 1048000`, `maxTokens: 32000`, and cost `{ input: 1, output: 4.05, cacheRead: 0.17, cacheWrite: 0 }`.\n- The same transcript fed a supported canonical row with `context_length: \"64000\"`, `max_completion_tokens: 4000`, and decimal prices `\"0.0000002\"`, `0.0000008`, and `\"0.00000004\"`; the projected model applied live values `contextWindow: 64000`, `maxTokens: 4000`, and cost `{ input: 0.2, output: 0.8, cacheRead: 0.04, cacheWrite: 0 }`.\n- Transcript assertions passed: `malformedFallsBack: true` and `supportedDecimalApplies: true`.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/baseten/models.test.ts` passed: 1 test file, 7 tests.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- GitHub Actions `Real behavior proof`, `openclaw/ci-gate`, `check-lint`, `check-prod-types`, `check-test-types`, and `check-additional-extension-package-boundary` passed for the current head.",
        "branch": "qingminlong/baseten-strict-live-model-numbers-v2",
